# Desktop-only UI

DoubleCheck is a **desktop local developer tool**. Do not add mobile layouts or responsive redesigns.

## Do not

- Add `@media (max-width: …)` breakpoints that restack or simplify the workspace for phones/tablets
- Add mobile navigation, hamburger menus, touch-only patterns, or “mobile-first” rewrites
- Change the layout viewport back to `width=device-width` for a phone-optimized layout
- Spend time on mobile polish, a11y-for-small-screens, or adaptive column collapse

## Do

- Keep a single desktop composition (wide grids, side panels, sticky detail panes)
- Prefer fixed desktop widths/padding over viewport-driven collapse
- If a layout breaks when the window is narrow, that is acceptable — do not add a mobile mode

`prefers-reduced-motion` is fine; phone-specific layout is not.
